## 4. Types of Recursion

| Type | Description | Example |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Tail Recursion** | Recursive call is the very last operation performed before returning. Can be optimized by compilers. | `return helper(n - 1, acc * n);` |
| **Head Recursion** | Recursive call is made before any other computation/processing in the function. | Calling `func(n - 1)` then printing `n`. |
| **Tree Recursion** | Function makes two or more recursive calls within its body (branches like a tree). | Fibonacci: `fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)` |
| **Indirect Recursion** | Function A calls Function B, and Function B calls Function A. | Mutual recursion |

