## 8. Recursion vs. Iteration

| Feature | Recursion | Iteration (Loops) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Basic Structure** | Function calls itself | Loop structures (`for`, `while`, `do-while`) |
| **Termination** | Triggered by base case | Triggered when condition evaluates to `false` |
| **Memory Overhead** | Higher (creates stack frame for each call) | Minimal ($\mathcal{O}(1)$ auxiliary space) |
| **Execution Speed** | Slower (function call overhead) | Faster (direct register/CPU jumps) |
| **Code Readability** | Cleaner for tree/graph traversal, divide & conquer | Can be longer or more verbose for hierarchical problems |
| **Risk** | Stack Overflow if too deep | Infinite loop (CPU consumption) |

